>Does the Wizard always escape up stairs?

Perhaps a minor spoiler....


In the game I just finished (h'ray!) when I was on my way up with the
Amulet, you-know-who came back.  He didn't get around to stealing the
Amulet from me...but when he got low on HP, he zapped a wand of digging
at the floor and escaped *down* a level!

I never saw him again, not even in the Endgame.

Perhaps this is (a) a useful tactic to get rid of the Wiz, ie. provide him
with a wand of digging and let him take himself out of the picture; and/or
(b) something for the dev team to fix.

Other notes (I'm playing 3.1.0 on Linux 0.99pl2) --

The Sanctum would be a lot harder if those priests of Moloch were
disintegration-resistant.  Not much of a challenge considering that you've
probably found a wand of death or two by the time you get there.

The Astral plane was absolutely trivial, and I'm very confused about
why.  When I arrived, I read a scroll of magic mapping (no sense saving
it, obviously), and for the Gehennom of it (so to speak) I decided to
zap myself with a wand of teleportation.

It worked.  It shouldn't have, but it worked.

Has anyone else encountered this?  Obviously the noteleport flag should
be set for the endlevels (and of course endgame.des indicates this).
And yet the game allowed me to teleport.  A few zaps later and I was at
the right altar with no Apocalyptic Horsemen in sight.

I've tested this inasmuch as I could (although it's tricky trying
to troubleshoot this sort of thing in wizard mode, since you can
teleport in wizard mode no matter where you are; instead I gave a
wand of teleportation to a monster and let him try to use it on
himself) and it seems that teleportation is allowed in all of the
endgame levels.  Is it just my system or does this happen elsewhere?

To test... in wizard mode, wish for the Amulet; go up the stairs into
the endgame; wish for a wand of teleportation; drop it; create a
monster (a nice hill giant will do); step away from the wand to let
the monster pick up the wand; then beat on him slowly until he tries
to zap himself with the wand.  If 'a mysterious force prevents the
hill giant from teleporting', then it's just me; if he teleports
or 'feels disoriented for a moment', it's a bug.

Dev team?

